<title>UK: Mexico sets 500 bln lire 10-year bond, +192 bp.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets 500 bln lire 10-year bond, +192 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Chase Manhattan International and Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MEXICO</p>
<p> AMT    500 BLN LIRE  COUPON     9.125     MATURITY    20.FEB.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.80    PAY DATE    20.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.40     SPREAD	+192 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BB	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BA2	 DENOMS (M) 5	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT/MX</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  MEXICO    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 8.75 BTP DUE 2006</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
